SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] October 31\, 2025: Annual Report for Fiscal Y
 ear 2025 now available
DESCRIPTION:Maine Human Rights Commission \n2025 Annual Report \nJuly 1\, 
 2024 - June 30\, 2025 \nMaine Human Rights Commission \n51 State House Sta
 tion\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/mhrc \n \n \n \n  \n \n \n  \
 n    \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n            \n             \n \n  \n \n
    \nPage| 2  \nTABLE OF CONTENTS \nLetter of Transmittal 3 \nOrigin\, Jur
 isdiction\, and Members of the Commission 5 \nProcess 6 \nStaffing 6 \nBud
 get 6 \nCase Activity \nComplaints Filed 7 \nCases Closed Before Commissio
 n Determination 8 \nHearings Determinations 8 \nReasonable Grounds Rates 9
  \nPost Reasonable Grounds Conciliations 9 \nLitigation 9 \nConclusion 9 \
 nMaine Human Righ ts \,Commi ssion \n51 Stat e House Station\, Augusta\, M
 aine 04333 \nPhone {20 7) 624 -629 0 • F ax {20 7) 6 24- 8 72 9 • ME R
 e]ay 711 \nwww . mai ne .. gov /mhrc \nPage| 3 \nKit Thomson Crossman \nEX
 ECUTIVE DIRECTOR \nBarbara Archer Hirsch \nCOMMISSION COUNSEL \nOctober 31
 \, 2025 \nThe Honorable Janet Mills\, Governor \nThe Honorable Matthea Dau
 ghtry\, President of the Maine Senate \nThe Honorable Ryan Fecteau\, Speak
 er of the Maine House of Representatives \nState House\, Augusta\, Maine 0
 4333 \nDear Governor Mills\, President Daughtry\, and Speaker Fecteau: \nO
 n behalf of the Commissioners and staff of the Maine Human Rights Commissi
 on (“Commission”)\, we are pleased \nto present you with our agency’
 s Fiscal Year 2025 (“FY 2025”) Annual Report. \nThe first half of FY 2
 025 was fairly uneventful. Commission staff worked hard to process\, inves
 tigate\, and close \ncases within the jurisdictional bounds of the Maine H
 uman Rights Act (“MHRA”)\, as well as the requirements of our \ntwo fe
 deral work-sharing agreements with the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity C
 ommission (“EEOC”) and the \nU.S. Department of Housing and Urban Deve
 lopment (“HUD”). This is work about which our staff is deeply \nknowle
 dgeable\, and over the more than 50 years of the Commission’s existence\
 , we have crafted policies and \nprocedures to ensure all Commission decis
 ions are made with rigor and integrity. \nEEOC interpret\nhttps://www.main
 e.gov/mhrc/sites/mhrc/files/inline-files/MHRC%20FY25%20Annual%20Report.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/mhrc/sites/mhrc/files/inline-files/MHRC%20FY25%2
 0Annual%20Report.pdf
