DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Section 90: Quarter 3\, Physician Drug and Se
 asonal Flu Code Update: CR 142091\, 142074
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Section 90: Quarter 3\, Physician Drug and Seasonal Flu
  Code Update: CR 142091\, 142074\nSection 90: Quarter 3\, Physician Drug a
 nd Seasonal Flu Code Update: CR 142091\, 142074\nSep 02\, 2026\nQTR 3 Phys
 ician Drug Codes\nTo align with the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Servi
 ces’ (CMS) quarterly rate update\, we updated the Physician Drug Rate
 s retroactively to July 1\, 2026. We implemented these new rates for bil
 ling on August 26\, 2026.\nYou can find the\nupdated rates\non the Rate S
 etting page of the Health PAS Online Portal.\nWe will reprocess claims su
 bmitted at or above the new rates\, for dates of service July 1\, 2025
 \, through August 25\, 2026.\nNo provider action is needed.\nSeasonal Flu
  Codes\nEffective August 1\, 2026\, MaineCare updated the seasonal flu cod
 es. We implemented these new rates for billing on August 26\, 2026.\nThe 
 new rates are provided in the table below.\nStart Date\nProcedure Code\nRa
 te\n8/1/2026\n90653\n$122.52\n8/1/2026\n90656\n$23.89\n8/1/2026\n90657\n$1
 1.14\n8/1/2026\n90658\n$22.28\n8/1/2026\n90660\n$30.58\n8/1/2026\n90661\n$
 66.57\n8/1/2026\n90662\n$122.52\n8/1/2026\n90673\n$122.52\nAdjustment Bill
 ing Guidance for Dates of Service July 1\, 2026 - August 25\, 2026\nMaine
 Care will adjust paid claims that were submitted with charges\nat or
  above\nthe new rates.\nProviders are responsible for adjusting claims
  submitted with charges\nbelow\nthe new rates. Per policy\, and to avoid
  timely filing denials\, adjustments must be submitted within 120 days
  of the most recent claim payment date.\nFor questions\, please contact y
 our\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/prov
 iders/provider-bulletins/section-90-quarter-3-physician-drug-and-seasonal-
